      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/egypt-lina-attalah-mada-masr-press-freedom-clampdown</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Warnings of escalating clampdown on press freedom come after Cairo court convicts Attalah of managing an unlicensed website&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Lina Attalah, a prominent Egyptian journalist and the editor-in-chief of the news outlet Mada Masr, has been released from detention by Egypt’s authorities and had her website ordered to be shut down by a court amid an intensifying crackdown on independent media in the country.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Attalah was taken briefly into custody after a Cairo court convicted her of managing an unlicensed website, prompting fresh international concerns over press freedom in Egypt.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/world/2026/oct/28/egypt-lina-attalah-mada-masr-press-freedom-clampdown"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
