      <title>Brazil publishes first global ‘roadmap’ for phasing out fossil fuels</title>
      <link>https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/03/brazil-first-global-roadmap-phasing-out-fossil-fuels</link>
      <description>&lt;p&gt;Cop30 host sets out steps to break link with coal, oil and gas as it aims to move focus from negotiating to implementing&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;All countries can start to break their dependence on fossil fuels now without needing to wait for new technologies or economic changes, Brazil’s government has said ahead of a global climate summit.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;Brazil, the host of &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2025/nov/25/fossil-fuel-giants-finally-in-the-crosshairs-cop30-avoids-total-failure-with-last-ditch-deal"&gt;last year’s UN climate conference&lt;/a&gt;, set out the world’s first global “roadmap” for phasing out fossil fuels on Tuesday, showing that countries could boost their economies and pull people out of poverty while breaking the link with coal, oil and gas.&lt;/p&gt; &lt;a href="https://www.theguardian.com/environment/2026/nov/03/brazil-first-global-roadmap-phasing-out-fossil-fuels"&gt;Continue reading...&lt;/a&gt;</description>
